Z||000002||Gold-86SE||01-24-2001||10:18 AM||||<BR>Adam, I think I have an idea of what you are trying to describe but, I think might might also be confused.<P>First you have an Automatic, and I am more familiar with Manuals.  However, it appears that you are trying to describe the portion of the console that physically holds the small metal ashtrays which is basically the shifter cover/plate. Is this correct?<P>For the most part the center console is constucted with these parts:<BR>  radio and evironmental control pod<BR>  extra gauges on top of pod (86-88 V6 only)<BR>  the glove box, which extends most of the length of the console<BR>  the shifter cover/plate<BR>  the plastic skelton on which all of this bolts<P>Hope this helped.<P>BTW, welcome to the forum.<BR><P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)<BR>Please visit my <A HREF="http://www.trifocus.net/~fws/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Work Shop</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||01-24-2001||04:06 PM||||Are you referring to the transmission selection indicator?<BR>If you are there should a white piece that's aprox. 3" wide and 4.5" long. under the shifter boot, there shoud be a gap that's about 1" wide and open at the front end. Inside this gap is a square piece that has an arm to the indicator window. It should hav retangular hole in the center of it though whice the shifter should pass through. This piece is free to slide the entire length of the opening (the slot).<BR>Hope this is it and provides you with assistance!<P>(shess!)  LUCK!||||reg||1
